<h2>Why Grind Size Matters So Much</h2>

<p>
  Grind size controls <strong>surface area</strong>. Finer grounds expose more surface to water, so extraction happens faster. Coarser grounds expose less, so extraction happens slower. Every brew method is designed around a specific contact time, and the grind size needs to match it.
</p>

<p>
  Use the wrong grind and you'll either under-extract (sour, thin) or over-extract (bitter, harsh). This is the #1 reason people's home coffee doesn't taste like the café's, and it's the easiest thing to fix.
</p>

